Even he suggests that certain abilities to interpret human behavior may exist in animals such as domesticated dogs.
Research from the 20th century has shown that there are two types of genetic variation: one hidden and the other visible.
Modification includes modern genetic alterations, and selection eliminates them from the pool of expressed variations.
Throughout each generation, there have been ongoing fluctuations between separation and integration among the two groups.
For gorillas, which have a human-like digestive system, it is difficult to meet their amino acid requirements from available plant resources in the wide savannas outside.
Moreover, failing to do so can have dangerous consequences: reduced growth, malnutrition, and ultimately death.
